  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 1, 'Hold a warm mug in both hands this morning and drink it slowly, with nothing else in front of you.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 2, 'Settle into your seat before work or study today, take one easy breath, and begin with a single small task.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 3, 'Turn your phone face down on the table the next time someone sits down to talk with you.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 4, 'Step outside your door for two minutes and feel the air on your face, doing nothing else.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 5, 'Choose the one thing that matters most today and write it on a small card you can see.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 6, 'Wash the dishes tonight with the radio and screens off, feeling the warm water and one plate at a time.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 7, 'Close every browser tab but one for the next fifteen minutes, and work only in that window.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 8, 'Look at the face of the person speaking to you for the whole of one short conversation today.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 9, 'Take a short walk this morning with no headphones, and listen to the sounds around you.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 10, 'Make a list of only three tasks for this morning and keep the longer list out of sight.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 11, 'Fold one basket of laundry without a screen nearby, smoothing each piece flat before you reach for the next.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 12, 'Finish writing one email and send it before you open the next one.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 13, 'Invite someone to teach you a small thing they love, like a knot or a recipe, and watch their hands as they show you.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 14, 'Stretch your arms overhead slowly and feel each part of the stretch from fingers to shoulders.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 15, 'Keep a scrap of paper beside you, and when a stray thought pops up, jot it down to come back to later.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 16, 'Make your bed slowly this morning, pulling each corner straight and noticing the feel of the sheets.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 17, 'Set a timer for twenty five minutes and give it to a single task, letting every other thought wait its turn.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 18, 'Let a friend finish their whole sentence before you begin your answer, even if you already know what you want to say.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 19, 'Let your shower be just a shower tonight: when plans start running in your head, come back to the warm water.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 20, 'Group your small errands together and do them in one trip this afternoon.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 21, 'Tidy just one room today, and leave the others alone until that room is done.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 22, 'Pause your chat notifications for half an hour this morning, and let your team know you will reply after.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 23, 'Play with your pet for five minutes this morning with nothing in your other hand.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 24, 'Rub a sprig of mint, rosemary or basil between your fingers and breathe in, noticing only the scent.'),
  ('doing-one-thing-at-a-time', 25, 'Shop one aisle at a time at the grocery store, finishing that part of your list before you move to the next.'),
